⚙️ systemctl vs journalctl
systemctl

systemctl is used to manage and check Linux services.

Example:

systemctl status ssh

It can be used to:

Check service status
Start services
Stop services
Restart services
Enable services
journalctl

journalctl is used to view system and service logs.

Example:

journalctl -u ssh

It can help investigate:

Service errors
Authentication events
Service activity
System events
Memory
systemctl
↓
